{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "libraryVersion": "1.2.0",
  "workflows": [
    {
      "id": "intake-and-triage",
      "title": "Intake and Triage",
      "description": "Capture the request, scope, urgency, handling constraints, initial evidence, and triage decision.",
      "introducedIn": "1.3.0",
      "defaultFolder": "02 Investigations",
      "body": [
        "## Content",
        "",
        "### Request",
        "",
        "**Requester:**",
        "",
        "**Received (UTC):**",
        "",
        "**Decision or intelligence need:**",
        "",
        "### Scope and urgency",
        "",
        "| In scope | Out of scope | Deadline | Priority |",
        "|---|---|---|---|",
        "|  |  |  |  |",
        "",
        "### Handling and authorization",
        "",
        "- [ ] Markings and dissemination constraints recorded.",
        "- [ ] Collection and analysis are authorized.",
        "- [ ] Sensitive or personal data requirements recorded.",
        "",
        "### Initial evidence",
        "",
        "| Item | Source | Observed (UTC) | Reliability |",
        "|---|---|---|---|",
        "|  |  |  |  |",
        "",
        "### Triage decision",
        "",
        "**Decision:** Accept / Defer / Redirect / Close",
        "",
        "**Rationale:**",
        "",
        "**Owner:**",
        "",
        "**Next action:**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ioc-and-observable-triage",
      "title": "IOC and Observable Triage",
      "description": "Normalize an indicator or observable, record provenance, assess validity, and decide its operational disposition.",
      "introducedIn": "1.3.0",
      "defaultFolder": "02 Investigations",
      "body": [
        "## Content",
        "",
        "### Submitted value",
        "",
        "**Raw value:**",
        "",
        "**Observable type:**",
        "",
        "**Submitted by / source:**",
        "",
        "**First received (UTC):**",
        "",
        "### Normalization",
        "",
        "| Normalized value | Transformation | Validation result |",
        "|---|---|---|",
        "|  |  |  |",
        "",
        "### Provenance and context",
        "",
        "- Original report or event:",
        "- Collection method:",
        "- First seen / last seen:",
        "- Source reliability:",
        "- Known handling restrictions:",
        "",
        "### Assessment",
        "",
        "| Question | Finding | Confidence |",
        "|---|---|---|",
        "| Is the value technically valid? |  |  |",
        "| Is it benign, suspicious, or malicious? |  |  |",
        "| Is it current and actionable? |  |  |",
        "| Could it cause false positives? |  |  |",
        "",
        "### Disposition",
        "",
        "**Decision:** Promote / Monitor / Enrich / Suppress / Reject",
        "",
        "**Reason:**",
        "",
        "**Expiry or review date:**",
        "",
        "**Detection or collection follow-up:**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pivot-and-enrichment-log",
      "title": "Pivot and Enrichment Log",
      "description": "Record each local or external pivot, its inputs, returned facts, provenance, limitations, and resulting leads.",
      "introducedIn": "1.3.0",
      "defaultFolder": "02 Investigations",
      "body": [
        "## Content",
        "",
        "### Starting point",
        "",
        "**Investigation question:**",
        "",
        "**Seed object or observable:**",
        "",
        "### Enrichment activity",
        "",
        "| Time (UTC) | Input | Source or tool | Query or method | Result | Confidence |",
        "|---|---|---|---|---|---|",
        "|  |  |  |  |  |  |",
        "",
        "### Provenance and limitations",
        "",
        "| Result | Provider or source | Retrieved (UTC) | License or handling | Limitation |",
        "|---|---|---|---|---|",
        "|  |  |  |  |  |",
        "",
        "### New leads",
        "",
        "| Lead | Why it matters | Owner | Status |",
        "|---|---|---|---|",
        "|  |  |  | Open |",
        "",
        "### Rejected pivots",
        "",
        "Record dead ends, duplicate results, rate limits, and reasons a result was not retained.",
        "",
        "### Analyst assessment",
        "",
        "Separate retrieved facts from inference and state what changed in the investigation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "analytic-timeline",
      "title": "Analytic Timeline",
      "description": "Order observed events, reported events, and analytic milestones while preserving source time, confidence, and uncertainty.",
      "introducedIn": "1.3.0",
      "defaultFolder": "02 Investigations",
      "body": [
        "## Content",
        "",
        "### Time boundaries",
        "",
        "**Earliest relevant time:**",
        "",
        "**Latest relevant time:**",
        "",
        "**Default timezone:** UTC",
        "",
        "### Events",
        "",
        "| Time (UTC) | Time type | Event | Objects | Source | Confidence |",
        "|---|---|---|---|---|---|",
        "|  | Observed / Reported / Inferred |  |  |  |  |",
        "",
        "### Ordering uncertainty",
        "",
        "Record approximate times, conflicting timestamps, clock skew, collection delay, and unresolved sequence questions.",
        "",
        "### Analytic milestones",
        "",
        "| Time (UTC) | Decision or judgment | New evidence | Analyst |",
        "|---|---|---|---|",
        "|  |  |  |  |",
        "",
        "### Key sequence assessment",
        "",
        "Explain the most important ordering, duration, gaps, and causal claims without presenting inference as observation."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
